      ":question/problem": "Express $\\frac{6}{5}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-\\frac{3}{5}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{6}{5}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-\\frac{3}{5}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{5}\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{5\\pi}{9}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{10\\pi}{9}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{5}\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{9}\\right)-1\\right)&=\\frac{3}{5}\\cos\\left(\\frac{10\\pi}{9}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
